  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Updated to Strengthening Humanitarian Assistance to Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) in Somalia through Improved Targeting and Monitoring</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia has been facing severe and escalating challenges due to conflicts and climate change, including recurrent droughts, floods, and extreme weather events. Against a protracted mass displacement backdrop, the number of vulnerable internally displaced persons (IDPs) in need of basic humanitarian assistance has been alarmingly increasing and the Post Delivery Aid Diversion (PDAD) has become growingly prevalent. This project aims to address these critical issues by: 1) continuing the scale-up of its Remote Monitoring Team (RMT) through the recruitment of Somali diaspora consultants with enumerator and data collection experience. The RMT supports rapid beneficiary verification through remote and; 2) continuing to expand its Biometric Registration and Verification (BRaVe) system through the registration of the targeted populations. This enables biometric registration, contributing to accurate identification and registration of beneficiaries, and a subsequent more efficient and effective aid delivery system.</narrative>
  </description>
